    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8682",
      "problem": "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14163649/assets/ef9e1dfd559c1e8818f14e100e07ab36ca167a4bd2ddf970bf3f5ef325103d64.png)",
      "worked_solution": "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14163649/assets/d4d61cf87f2c62c5cf4727384d6dfcc05cada6b23025dd6dd674130eaf64dd45.png)",
